;; itonami.cloud deployment profile.
;;
;; Application sessions are Passkey-only. Provider OAuth is reserved for
;; delegated service connections; Email and provider SSO cannot mint an app
;; session even when an older resident configuration still contains settings
;; for them.
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; Bots run on murakumo's OpenRouter-backed flash models (owner instruction
;; 2026-08-30: stabilize like Grok Bots / Hermes Agent; pay x402 USDC; consume
;; credits). They talk only to api.murakumo.cloud. They do not hold an
;; OpenRouter key.
;;
;; Grok Bots survive by dereferencing the `murakumo-main` alias. Hermes
;; measured 2026-08-30 that `z-ai/glm-5.3-flash` is the primary that actually
;; completes (56 ok / 7 fail) and that the OpenRouter free router is worse.
;; Standing on `openrouter/free` from this profile (ADR-2608272200) was the
;; 77% failure mode: pinned free ids die in ~24h.
;;
;; Routing, after the gateway is configured:
;;   z-ai/glm-5.3-flash → qwen/qwen3.8-flash → murakumo-main
;; Identity is MURAKUMO_API_KEY (shared token). That is the operator rail —
;; credits debit identified customers, not this token (double-charge vs
;; OpenRouter, and a zero wallet would 402 Domain Steward).
;;
;; This is the operator's act of reviewing, which is the only place it can
;; happen: `resources/cloud-itonami-app.defaults.edn` ships every destination
;; that leaves the machine as `:reviewed? false :enabled? false`.
;;
;;   MURAKUMO_API_KEY=<key> CLOUD_ITONAMI_PROFILE=itonami clojure -M:server
{:auth {:allow-signup? true}
 :cloud-relay {:base-url "https://hooks.itonami.cloud"
               :access-token-env "CLOUD_ITONAMI_RELAY_ACCESS_TOKEN"}
 :bots {:mail-domain "mail.itonami.cloud"
        :workforce {:model "z-ai/glm-5.3-flash"}}
 :providers [{:id "murakumo"
              :enabled? true
              :reviewed? true
              :default-model "z-ai/glm-5.3-flash"
              :max-transient-retries 2}
             {:id "openrouter" :enabled? false}]
 :routing {:default-provider "murakumo"
           :default-model "z-ai/glm-5.3-flash"
           :cloud-enabled? true}}
